WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.400
There’s something out there, stalking, watching,
lying in wait for the right moment.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.330
It can be anywhere, disappear in the blink
of an eye and reappear somewhere else, always

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.400
poised and ready to strike.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.529
The SCP Foundation has it locked up for now;
they keep a tracking tag fixed to it so they

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:21.770
can find it whenever it gets out.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.390
And believe us, it does get out.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:30.839
So, when it does, you should watch your back,
keep your wits about you, and check over your

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:32.770
shoulder if you hear something move.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.150
If you aren’t careful, it might come for
you.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:41.300
If you let your guard slip, even just for
a second, you could be next…

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.390
Mclean, Virginia - It’s hardly a hotbed
of anomalous activity, Viola thought to herself

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.170
as she pulled up at the unassuming townhouse.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:55.120
When she first joined the SCP Foundation,
Field Agent Smythe had imagined her life to

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:01.739
be full of adventure, battling anomalous monsters
and entities with the power to rewrite reality

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:02.739
itself.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:07.790
Instead, she had unwittingly pulled a short
straw somewhere along the way, and now got

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.300
saddled with this: retrieving an anomaly that
had gone missing.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.640
Viola had no idea what to expect, all she
had been told was that, according to its tracking

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:24.630
tag, the anomaly had teleported into one of
three Potential Relocation Sites, or PRSs.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.549
She just happened to be the closest available
Field Agent station nearby, and was instructed

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:33.770
to drive over and collect it and return the
escaped SCP to the Foundation.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:39.090
They had told Agent Smythe it was harmless,
putting her guard right down as she stepped

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.850
inside the house.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.079
She wasn’t prepared for the ambush that
awaited her…

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:49.560
The house – codenamed PRS ‘Townhouse’
– was silent, practically abandoned as she

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.930
made her sweep.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:57.770
Room by room, Viola was methodically checking
her corners, looking under beds, inside cupboards,

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:03.250
behind couches, on top of shelves, making
sure she’d covered every single inch of

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.360
the house.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.000
Whatever this anomaly was, it was good at
hiding.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.330
Before long, Agent Smythe had checked the
whole house from top to bottom and had found

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.820
nothing, no sight of the elusive SCP.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.610
With no idea where it was, Viola went into
the kitchen; she figured she might as well

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.330
see if there was anything to eat in this place.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:28.140
Maybe it had already gone, she thought; she’d
have to check in with base, and see if the

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.070
tracking tag was still active at this location.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:36.970
This thing could teleport, after all, it could
be sunbathing in Cancun by now, drinking a

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.770
Pina Colada out of a coconut with a tiny umbrella.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.430
Oh, wouldn’t that be the life…

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.010
Viola approached the refrigerator and casually
placed her hand on the door.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:51.900
With no idea what was waiting for her inside,
she pulled it open… and was immediately

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.770
hit in the face with a pillow.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:59.780
It wasn’t traveling at any substantial speed,
in fact, it was like it had been lightly thrown

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.500
by a human hand more than anything else.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.610
It didn’t knock Field Agent Smythe back
or send her reeling, or have enough force

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.060
to cause any injury.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:13.220
Instead, the pillow just softly impacted Viola’s
face, giving a little ‘squeak’ like a

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.970
dog toy would before it lazily fell onto the
kitchen floor.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:21.210
Fixed to one side of it was a post-it note
with a crudely drawn face that glared up at

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.670
her with a jagged frown.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:26.850
Viola sighed, mildly annoyed that she’d
just had a pillow thrown at her now, after

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.050
having spent a half-hour searching the house.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:35.520
Leaning down, she picked it up, and radioed
the Foundation; she’d found SCP-3832.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.310
But it didn’t end there, oh no.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:44.310
After they got the anomaly safely back in
its containment locker, it wasn’t long before

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:48.880
the Foundation was soon inundated with more
pillowy pandemonium.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:55.640
Nobody was safe from being the next victim
of a sudden ambush by SCP-3832, not even a

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.000
harmless, unassuming researcher like Doctor
Franklin Prangley.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.020
He had just been going about his day, checking
containment procedures were all in place,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:09.840
running tests on a few SCPs, the usual stuff
for a scientist working at Site 64.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:16.510
That was when the call went out over the comms
system: it had happened again, SCP-3832 had

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:19.940
vanished from the locker it was usually kept
secure in.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.720
While, on the outside, it looked like little
more than an ordinary cushion, this anomaly

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.810
was the ultimate hunter, displaying behavior
almost exactly like that of various highly

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.510
evolved ambush predators in the wild.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:38.530
And now, this hunter was loose again, and
it was open season on the Foundation staff.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:43.550
This time, it hadn’t gone far, having only
teleported to a different part of Site 64.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:48.870
As he would soon discover, the cunning cushion
was hiding just above Doctor Prangley’s

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.900
locker, waiting for the researcher to return
to his office.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:56.790
Then, when he was close enough, SCP-3832 would
strike.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.540
But the next would-be victim of the predatory
pillow had an advantage.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:06.460
The location tracking tag that the Foundation
had affixed to the pillow proved to be its

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:11.070
downfall, giving Prangley an approximate fix
on its whereabouts.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:15.940
Gently pushing his office door open, he instantly
spotted it on the top of his office locker,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.450
ready to pounce on him the moment he got close
enough.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:24.790
Slowly and methodically, Doctor Prangley edged
around his office, reaching for a meterstick

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.370
he kept by his desk.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:32.000
With his chosen weapon in hand, the Foundation
researcher stepped closer to his locker, eyes

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.130
fixed on SCP-3832.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:40.050
He was brandishing the wooden meterstick in
both hands, carrying it like an early caveman

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.570
with a hand-crafted spear.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:46.220
At that moment, Doctor Franklin Prangley was
locked in the dichotomy between predator and

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:53.250
prey, that age-old dance, a battle that had
raged for almost all of time itself: man versus

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.250
pillow.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.860
We’ve all been there, haven’t we?

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:02.220
Suddenly, striking first, Franklin took a
sharp swipe at SCP-3832 with his meterstick.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:06.960
He broke out with a smile of glee as the pillow
was toppled from its vantage point; it no

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.010
longer had the high ground over him.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:14.800
Employing a swift offense as the best defense,
the noble Doctor Prangley had felled SCP-3832

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:19.750
in one quick, pre-emptive strike… or so
he thought.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:23.680
As the old saying goes, “Pride goeth before
the fall.”

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:29.880
No sooner had it landed in a heap on the office
floor, than SCP-3832 launched itself back

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.200
up and limply hit Franklin square in the stomach.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:38.240
He let out a low grunt as the pillow connected
with his lower abdomen, and squeaked again,

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.230
announcing to the world that SCP-3832 had
just claimed its latest victim.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.770
Dr. Prangley might never get over that particular
humiliation.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:51.980
If he’s eaten by SCP-682 in a week, it will
be a merciful reprieve.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:58.070
No one could end this crafty cushion’s reign
of terror, to stand against this goose feather-filled

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.570
hunter was to risk certain death…

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:03.830
well, death by embarrassment, at least.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:07.360
Which some would argue is honestly worse.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.010
Security Officer Jennifer Blaire was never
the same after it happened to her.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:15.750
It was waiting for her behind the coffee machine
in the Site 64 break room.

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:19.919
She’d gone in there for a quick cup, just
to recharge her energy levels with a boost

00:07:19.919 --> 00:07:24.560
of caffeine before getting back to her post
guarding the containment level.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:28.330
Poor Jen, she never saw it coming.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:33.460
SCP-3832 leaped from its latest hiding place,
striking Officer Blaire right in her unprotected

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:34.460
ankle.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.830
The sudden, vicious attack from the polyester
cover-wearing persecutor caught her completely

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:44.210
unguarded, which was somewhat ironic for a
member of the Foundation’s security personnel.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:48.260
But Security Officer Jennifer Blake had no
time to laugh at the irony there.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:52.870
Punctuated by that same squeaking sound, the
sudden impact of the pillow colliding with

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.060
her ankle caused her to stumble.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:08:00.360
Not fall, mind you, she only lost balance
on one leg and was able to quickly steady

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.070
herself immediately after.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:06.910
But it was enough, just enough… for her
coffee to spill!

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:11.160
If you need a moment to compose yourself after
that horrifying revelation, we’d understand,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:16.230
it’s one of the more disturbing things we’ve
shared on this normally family-friendly channel.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:22.130
Leave a comment with the key phrase “#JusticeForJen”
so this poor SCP Foundation security officer

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:26.410
knows she’s in your thoughts and prayers
after this harrowing incident.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.410
Everyone okay now?

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.410
Good.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.580
Back to the story at hand.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:35.270
The incident caused Jen to suffer a few minor
first-degree burns on her hand and wrist,

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:40.159
requiring a fifteen-minute treatment in the
Site 64 infirmary - which the medic described

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:44.330
as “The worst relatively minor burns I’ve
ever seen.”

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.720
While her external injuries might not have
taken much time to heal, now Officer Blake

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.690
has to bring instant coffee from home to work
in a thermos flask.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:55.070
Can you imagine such horror?

00:08:55.070 --> 00:09:00.580
It stretches the human imagination to even
compensate for the level of terror it inspires

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.910
in our hearts and souls.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:08.560
Everywhere you looked, Site 64 staff were
being struck down left, right, and center,

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:16.410
mildly inconvenienced without warning by non-lethal
and mostly harmless ambushes from SCP-3832.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:21.430
During another relocation incident, the predatory
pillow teleported itself back to the location

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:25.100
known as PRS Townhouse in Mclean, Virginia.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:30.460
Once again, Field Agent Viola Smythe was dispatched
to the scene to retrieve the elusive pillow,

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:36.220
only this time, she had learned from her last
encounter: she’d brought backup.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:41.730
Specifically, one other Field Officer, named
Gordon Gompton, to hopefully give the cunning

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:44.300
cushion its critical comeuppance.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:48.660
Both field agents knew one of them would have
to take the hit, and Gordon stepped up to

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:49.660
the task.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:52.020
After all, it had already got Viola once before.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:57.550
It was his turn to face the nightmare that
was SCP-3832 head-on.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:02.520
They entered the townhouse, Agent Gompton
taking the lead, acting as a human shield

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:05.660
against any oncoming pillowy projectiles.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:11.990
Just as they expected, and as it had before,
the ambush took place not long after, with

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.500
SCP-3832 ineffectively hurling itself from
its hiding place.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:20.040
But, at the last possible second, Gordon ducked
out of the way.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:25.120
It was purely instinctive, but it left Viola
at the mercy of the oncoming cushion.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:31.340
It was a betrayal of truly Shakespearian proportions,
playing out in real-time.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:36.140
Marginally vexed at being hit a second time
with the pillow, Agent Smythe immediately

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:39.050
decided to claim her well-earned revenge.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:44.880
Grabbing the nearest safe object, which happened
to be SCP-3832 itself, she hurled it directly

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.060
at her fellow field operative.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:51.800
It collided with his head with another ‘squeak’,
the combined sight and sound causing Viola

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.550
to burst out laughing.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:57.360
Wearing a crafty smirk, Gordon grabbed the
pillow and threw it back at her, the same

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:58.360
thing happening.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:04.960
The pair of them kept at it, repeatedly throwing
SCP-3832 at each other again and again, every

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:10.540
time the same squeaking filled the air, followed
by more laughing from the two agents.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:16.550
As they continued their pillow fight, SCP-3832
underwent a change that nobody at the SCP

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:18.860
Foundation had ever witnessed before.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:24.060
With every throw, hitting either Agent Smythe
or Agent Gompton with its characteristic squeaking

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:30.050
noise, the face drawn on the post-it note
that was permanently stuck to SCP-3832 began

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:31.210
to change.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:36.120
Usually, the sticky paper depicted a jagged,
hand-drawn, frowny face; an upturned mouth

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:38.750
and eyebrows pointing inward in attack formation.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:42.590
A truly terrifying countenance to behold.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:46.779
It also turned out that it was impossible
to remove the post-it without causing the

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:48.250
pillow to teleport again.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:53.490
However, while it was being thrown about,
used in a pillow fight between two Foundation

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:58.700
field agents, joining in a rare moment of
childlike joy, the face of SCP-3832 began

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.700
to change.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:07.690
The frown was replaced with the unmistakable
curvature of a smile, those angry attack eyebrows

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:13.430
completely vanishing as the pillow was pleasantly
pelted from Agent Viola Smythe to Agent Gordon

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.430
Gompton.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:18.140
Eventually, after they’d had their fun,
the two operatives were duty-bound to return

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:20.240
the now-grinning cushion to Foundation.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:25.490
They reported their findings to researchers,
many of whom seemed eager to take part in

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:30.339
tests replicating this incident, either because
they were looking to blow off some steam with

00:12:30.339 --> 00:12:35.780
a nice, wholesome pillow fight, or because
they wanted to make SCP-3832 smile again.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:39.930
It didn’t take long for the fearsome piece
of feather-filled furniture to get back to

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:41.600
its old tricks though.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.500
After all, you can’t teach an old pillow
new tricks.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:47.690
And as for its next, unsuspecting victim?

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:54.190
The next would be none other than the Director
of Site 64 himself, one Edgar Holman.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:58.930
That’s right, not even one of the highest-ranked
members of Foundation staff stationed at that

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:03.450
particular facility was exempt from falling
prey to the dreaded pillow.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:09.200
Having once again disappeared from the confines
of its locker, SCP-3832 subsequently concealed

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:14.910
itself under the desk in Director Holman’s
office, laying in wait to pounce at its prey.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:18.930
As he pulled up his chair to sit down, the
site director was met with a soft, cushiony

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:24.320
impact to his shins; any further up and it
could’ve caused serious damage, he was lucky

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.620
that dastardly pillow didn’t crease his
well-ironed slacks!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:34.740
Then there was the relocation event that became
known as Incident 3832-NR1.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:40.980
A few key differences set this particular
occurrence apart from the others on SCP-3832’s

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:43.839
calamitous cacophony of concealed cushion
carnage.

00:13:43.839 --> 00:13:51.950
For one, it is what directly led to the first
of a few rare instances where the post-it-faced

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:57.310
pillow teleported itself to a location now
known as PRS ‘Truffle’, the designation

00:13:57.310 --> 00:14:01.670
given to St John’s Chocolate Factory in
Portland, Oregon.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:05.300
Why a Saint had a chocolate factory, we may
never know.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:06.660
But I digress.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:11.830
Since becoming a Potential Relocation Site
that SCP-3832 is able to transport itself

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:15.670
to, the factory had to be seized by the SCP
Foundation.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:20.140
Where it had once offered tours to the public
to present them with all the wonders of the

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:25.250
sweet-toothed process of making chocolate,
the gates now remained closed, with the false

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:30.690
promise that St John’s Chocolate Factory
was ‘Under New Management’, keeping people

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:31.690
out.

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:35.570
Entire floors that could easily be accessed
by someone trying to swipe a sample or two

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:39.990
have now been completely cleared out by the
Foundation, with not a stick of furniture

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:46.250
left in the place for anyone to steal, or
for SCP-3832 to hide behind.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:52.300
On the fourteenth of February, St Valentine’s
Day, 2017, Foundation technicians had been

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:57.300
working on repairing a glitch that had been
disrupting SCP-3832’s tracking tag.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:03.180
It was during that moment that the wily, polyester
pillow teleported out of its locker at Site

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:09.200
64 once again, vanishing and reappearing in
the trunk of a car belonging to a member of

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.200
personnel.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:14.320
Now, for security reasons, the name of this
staff member has been censored, letting her

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:19.250
retain her anonymity… and probably whatever
is left of her dignity too.

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:24.610
We’ll just call her Big Sister, which is
how the file on the highly classified SCP

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.959
Archive refers to her.

00:15:25.959 --> 00:15:32.029
Up until this point, the researchers at the
SCP Foundation had never known SCP-3832 to

00:15:32.029 --> 00:15:35.959
have the ability to teleport into a moving
vehicle.

00:15:35.959 --> 00:15:40.720
Teleportation is hard enough at the best of
times; seriously; you try shifting every atom

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:44.779
of your body from one spot to another without
getting stuck in a wall.

00:15:44.779 --> 00:15:49.839
And yet, the crafty cushion made the switch
effortlessly, relocating itself into the back

00:15:49.839 --> 00:15:52.829
of Big Sister’s car without her noticing.

00:15:52.829 --> 00:15:55.920
And to her credit, she had other things on
her mind.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:00.800
She’d just finished a long day’s work
at Site 64, and she still needed to pick something

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:04.620
up for a special someone; it was Valentine’s
Day after all.

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:09.649
As she drove away, Big Sister was completely
oblivious to the fact that SCP-3832 could

00:16:09.649 --> 00:16:13.400
apparently now teleport itself into moving
vehicles.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:17.350
The research team studying the pillow and
even the security staff she passed at the

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:20.100
front gate were equally unaware.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:25.630
Making her way further and further from Site
64, Big Sister pulled onto the freeway, nervously

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.350
checking her watch.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:31.910
She desperately hoped she could get there
in time before the factory closed, and that

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.050
they’d still have a box left.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.170
They had to, right?

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:37.330
Who sells out of chocolate on Valentine’s
Day?

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:42.630
It’s their biggest sales day of the year,
save for perhaps Easter Sunday.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:48.610
Getting closer to St John’s Chocolate Factory,
Big Sister could see from a distance that

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.610
the lights were still on.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:54.540
She relaxed in the driver’s seat, breathing
a sigh of relief that she’d made it in good

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.540
time.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:59.120
Her thoughts quickly turned to her sweetheart,
imagining the look of delight on their face

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:05.250
when she got home and presented them with
a shiny, heart-shaped box, filled with a delicious

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.910
assortment of confectionaries.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:10.919
Parking up, she dashed inside, the last person
in before closing time.

00:17:10.919 --> 00:17:16.449
Little did she know what was still lurking
in the trunk of her car - like the urban legend

00:17:16.449 --> 00:17:18.850
of the ax-wielding killer in the backseat.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:24.409
With her romantic holiday gesture of a box
of chocolates all paid for and tucked securely

00:17:24.409 --> 00:17:26.983
under her arm, Big Sister made her way back
to the car.

00:17:26.983 --> 00:17:31.610
Then, a thought struck her, a terrible thought…

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.080
she couldn’t just leave this in the car!

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:38.210
The surprise would be totally ruined if her
significant other could see what she’d got

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:39.210
for them.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:43.970
There was only one thing for it, the box of
chocolates needed to be hidden when she got

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:48.399
home, and where else do you think to hide
something in a car?

00:17:48.399 --> 00:17:50.759
In the trunk, of course.

00:17:50.759 --> 00:17:55.139
As Big Sister unlocked the back and lifted
up the trunk lid, a concealed cushion stealth

00:17:55.139 --> 00:17:58.320
attack of pure pillow force struck her.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:03.909
SCP-3832 launched itself from its hiding place,
only to collide with the box that Big Sis

00:18:03.909 --> 00:18:08.269
was carrying, catching her completely by surprise.

00:18:08.269 --> 00:18:12.899
Making its signature squeak, the predatory
pillow knocked the box sharply upwards into

00:18:12.899 --> 00:18:18.350
the air and, in a cruel twist of fate, sent
the pointed edge of the heart straight into

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.159
Big Sister’s face.

00:18:20.159 --> 00:18:25.970
The tapered tip was propelled straight into
her mouth, chipping her front tooth, as SCP-3832

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:28.340
landed on the ground of the parking lot.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:34.389
It was the most brutally violent attack that
SCP-3832 had ever conducted, shocking everyone

00:18:34.389 --> 00:18:38.720
at the SCP Foundation with its sheer wanton
ferocity.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:43.720
Making a call to the SCP Foundation, Big Sister
requested a recovery team to come and collect

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:48.239
the troublesome cushion; after picking up
the present for her Valentine and the fragment

00:18:48.239 --> 00:18:52.080
of her tooth it had rather unceremoniously
knocked out.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:57.760
Sighing, she leaned against the rear bumper
of her car, keeping an eye on SCP-3832 while

00:18:57.760 --> 00:18:59.549
she waited for the recovery team to arrive.

00:18:59.549 --> 00:19:04.909
What a way to spend Valentine’s Day, Big
Sister thought to herself, worried about what

00:19:04.909 --> 00:19:08.200
her partner would say when she got home late
with a chipped tooth.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:12.559
Then she noticed something that, while it
didn’t fix the situation, at least made

00:19:12.559 --> 00:19:14.940
her feel a little less bad about it.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:19.500
The post-it note face of SCP-3832 had changed
once again.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:23.630
Big Sister grabbed her phone from her pocket
to take a picture of it so she could hand

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:26.480
it over as evidence to the research team.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:33.239
Instead of its normal frown scribbled across
the sticky note, SCP-3832’s hand-drawn expression

00:19:33.239 --> 00:19:39.399
had become an almost bashful, dimpled smile,
with a big pair of cartoon hearts in its eyes.

00:19:39.399 --> 00:19:44.590
So, if you take anything away from this video,
it should be this gentle reminder.

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:49.070
The chances of you being ambushed and pounced
upon by pillow with a post-it note for a face

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.070
are…

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:53.710
well, statistically speaking, the chances
are pretty slim, But they’re never zero

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.090
either.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:59.909
You really should keep your wits about you,
stay alert, make sure you check for movement

00:19:59.909 --> 00:20:04.850
when you leave every room, and look under
tables and even in your refrigerator just

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:05.850
to be safe.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:10.249
And if you see something moving, out of the
corner of your eye, even just for a split

00:20:10.249 --> 00:20:16.249
second… then you too might just get hit
in the face by a pillow.

00:20:16.249 --> 00:20:21.070
Now, why not go and check out “SCP-999:
THE TICKLE MONSTER” and “SCP-348 A GIFT

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:25.440
FROM DAD” to get yourself acquainted with
a few of the more adorable anomalies that

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.639
the SCP Foundation have encountered!

